# Use-case 01 gap 8 (claim C1, inverse half): typing BOTH directions of
# an inverse relation pair with refer(t) dies of a spurious cycle.  The
# two targets are plain consistent maps ({kind: service} meets
# {kind: service} is a fixpoint), so the meet converges; unify_cycle is
# raised anyway.  Typing only ONE direction (bare refer() on the other)
# evaluates fine — that asymmetric workaround is what 01/spec.aon ships.
# expected: {"a":{"dependsOn":["svc/b"],"kind":"service"},
#            "b":{"dependedOnBy":["svc/a"],"kind":"service"}} exit 0
# actual:   [aontu/unify_cycle]: Cannot unify values at path $.b
#           (Cannot unify value: {"dependedOnBy":[...],"kind":"service"}
#            with value: {"kind":"service"}) exit 1
a: id(svc/a) & { kind: service, dependsOn:    [&: refer({kind: service}), svc/b] }
b: id(svc/b) & { kind: service, dependedOnBy: [&: refer({kind: service}), svc/a] }
